or high precision. To ensure the reliability of this automated evaluation and mitigate potential biases, we validate the SAM 3 detections against manual human annotations on a subset of the data. Our primary metrics include: Exact Match Accuracy (%): The percentage of object categories where the predicted count exactly matches the target count. Relative Tolerance Accuracy ( ± 10 % , ± 20 % \pm 10\%,\pm 20\% ): The percentage of object categories whose predicted count falls within a strict percentage-based error margin, scaling naturally with large object counts. Error Magnitude (MAE and RMSE): Mean Absolute Error measures the average absolute deviation between target and detected counts per category, while Root Mean Square Error disproportionately penalizes massive outlier failures (such as the fusion of many objects). 4.3 Comparison Against State-of-the-Arts Table 1 : OverlapDepth-45K ( 1,000 1{,}000 -image test): T2I vs. L2I under a fair layout protocol. Layout rows use identical LLM-inferred boxes and labels generated by Gemini 3 Flash ( Section 4.3 ). Accuracy (%) ↑ \uparrow Error ↓ \downarrow Method Type Exact ± 10 % \pm 10\% ± 20 % \pm 20\% MAE RMSE FLUX.2-Klein-4b (text only) T2I 13.24 18.18 30.59 5.21 9.96 SDXL-Turbo Podell et al. (2024) (text only) T2I 5.30 9.50 18.50 10.05 14.71 GLIGEN Li et al. (2023) L2I 8.84 15.48 29.15 11.41 18.76 MIGC Zhou et al. (2024) L2I 10.46 19.12 30.17 4.83 6.96 3DIS Zhou et al. (2025) L2I 12.88 19.48 30.17 4.07 6.34 AIBL (Ours) L2I 15.32 20.12 33.11 3.89 5.99 Text-to-image vs. layout-to-image baselines on OverlapDepth-45K. Benchmarking mixes two confounds: whether a model receives explicit spatial anchors, and which boxes are supplied at test time. To ensure a fair comparison and separate paradigm differences from layout-quality bias, Table 1 contrasts text-to-image (T2I) systems that only observe the revised count prompts against layout-to-image (L2I) systems that additionally receive the same LLM-inferred layout boxes (genera